WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.099 --> 00:00:06.049
How I Met Your Mother star Josh Radnor anchored
the CBS sitcom for nine seasons as the unlucky-in-love

00:00:06.049 --> 00:00:11.690
Ted Mosby, working his way into viewers' hearts
with his adorable smiles, constant optimism,

00:00:11.690 --> 00:00:13.410
and pretentious pronunciation skills.

00:00:13.410 --> 00:00:16.390
"Oh you think it should be pronounced encyclopedia?

00:00:16.390 --> 00:00:23.210
It's a common mistake, but if you look at
the squished together A-E symbol in this here encyclopedia,

00:00:23.210 --> 00:00:28.590
you'll learn that it's a ligature derived
from the Anglo-Saxon rune…"

00:00:28.590 --> 00:00:35.149
However, since the hit show ended in 2013,
Radnor has been noticeably missing from the

00:00:35.149 --> 00:00:36.149
limelight.

00:00:36.149 --> 00:00:39.899
Since so many people loved his character on
the series, everyone wants to know why he

00:00:39.899 --> 00:00:45.269
hasn't been in another other high-profile
projects, so let's explore why Hollywood won't cast

00:00:45.269 --> 00:00:46.999
Josh Radnor anymore.

00:00:46.999 --> 00:00:49.909
MIA at the movies

00:00:49.909 --> 00:00:53.719
Radnor didn't have very many credits to his
name before getting cast as the lead in How

00:00:53.719 --> 00:00:54.819
I Met Your Mother.

00:00:54.819 --> 00:00:59.109
Aside from a small appearance in Not Another
Teen Movie, he'd only had guest appearances

00:00:59.109 --> 00:01:00.670
on various TV shows.

00:01:00.670 --> 00:01:05.110
How I Met Your Mother launched him to stardom,
and his most notable role since then has been

00:01:05.110 --> 00:01:09.670
in the TV sphere, as Dr. Jed Foster on PBS'
Mercy Street.

00:01:09.670 --> 00:01:13.810
In other words, Radnor just hasn't shown that
he can anchor a film yet, which could make

00:01:13.810 --> 00:01:18.420
studios wary of casting him and risking poor
box office returns.

00:01:18.420 --> 00:01:20.640
Ted Mosby Eternal

00:01:20.640 --> 00:01:25.240
It's often tough for actors who spent a long
time playing one part to shed that identity.

00:01:25.240 --> 00:01:29.700
To many viewers, Sarah Michelle Gellar will
always be Buffy, Daniel Radcliffe will always

00:01:29.700 --> 00:01:33.630
be Harry Potter, and Josh Radnor will always
be Ted Mosby.

00:01:33.630 --> 00:01:37.810
This can make it difficult for actors to move
on from career-defining characters and can

00:01:37.810 --> 00:01:41.670
make it hard for casting directors to see
them in potential roles.

00:01:41.670 --> 00:01:43.759
Just ask Mark Hamill…

00:01:43.759 --> 00:01:45.259
Looking for love

00:01:45.259 --> 00:01:50.179
Like Ted Mosby, Radnor has ALSO been trying
his best to find Mrs. Right in real life.

00:01:50.179 --> 00:01:53.979
"If you're looking for the word that means
caring about someone beyond all rationality

00:01:53.979 --> 00:01:57.289
and wanting to have everything they want no
matter how much it destroys you…

00:01:57.289 --> 00:01:58.289
It's love."

00:01:58.289 --> 00:02:01.960
He hasn't married or made mysterious-mothered
children with anyone yet, but there have been

00:02:01.960 --> 00:02:04.619
plenty of rumors surrounding his partners.

00:02:04.619 --> 00:02:08.729
Radnor split with actress Lindsay Price, whom
he met on the set of How I Met Your Mother,

00:02:08.729 --> 00:02:10.840
after a year of dating in 2009.

00:02:10.840 --> 00:02:16.730
He was linked to Twilight actress Julia Jones
in 2013 and later dated actress Marisa Tomei

00:02:16.730 --> 00:02:18.380
in 2014.

00:02:18.380 --> 00:02:22.590
After that, reports say that he's dating Friday
Night Lights beauty Minka Kelly.

00:02:22.590 --> 00:02:26.920
If we learned anything from Ted, it's that
finding that special someone can involve a

00:02:26.920 --> 00:02:29.230
lot of trial and error.

00:02:29.230 --> 00:02:30.960
Tapping it out

00:02:30.960 --> 00:02:35.390
The actor is also working on other writing
projects that may keep him from screen work,

00:02:35.390 --> 00:02:40.950
including securing a deal for his as-yet-untitled
book on his attempts to "answer the big questions

00:02:40.950 --> 00:02:42.180
about spirituality."

00:02:42.180 --> 00:02:47.340
The book is expected to follow "an ongoing
quest that takes [Radnor] from his youth in

00:02:47.340 --> 00:02:52.840
heartland Ohio to the unexpected lessons of
celebrity and beyond."

00:02:52.840 --> 00:02:55.670
Tied up behind the lens

00:02:55.670 --> 00:03:01.200
Radnor won the Sundance Film Festival Dramatic
Audience Award for his 2010 directorial debut

00:03:01.200 --> 00:03:04.480
Happythankyoumoreplease, which he also wrote
and starred in.

00:03:04.480 --> 00:03:09.050
Since then, Radnor has also written, directed
and starred in the film Liberal Arts and is

00:03:09.050 --> 00:03:13.840
set to direct — but not star in — the
upcoming sci-fi drama The Leaves.

00:03:13.840 --> 00:03:19.500
Radnor said he got into writing with Happythankyoumoreplease
in order to "give [himself] a great film role,"

00:03:19.500 --> 00:03:23.870
adding that by writing, directing, and acting
in his films, he can create projects that

00:03:23.870 --> 00:03:25.450
feel personal.

00:03:25.450 --> 00:03:27.980
Dabbling in music

00:03:27.980 --> 00:03:33.010
Radnor is part of the band Radnor &amp; Lee, along
with Australian musician Ben Lee, and in October

00:03:33.010 --> 00:03:36.670
2016, Radnor announced that they were working
on a debut album:

00:03:36.670 --> 00:03:41.370
"So I understand you're writing songs for
your first album, that's great.

00:03:41.600 --> 00:03:44.100
"I am. I am..."

00:03:44.540 --> 00:03:46.200
"You play instruments?"

00:03:46.460 --> 00:03:50.240
"I do not play an instrument. I'm writing an album."

00:03:50.810 --> 00:03:52.260
"We're instrument-free as well."

00:03:52.260 --> 00:03:54.600
"We have a support group going."

00:03:54.600 --> 00:03:59.570
Called, "Love Songs for God and Women," Radnor
said the album will feature mellow folk songs

00:03:59.570 --> 00:04:01.600
co-written and performed by the duo.

00:04:01.600 --> 00:04:05.600
"We decided to write one song together and
we had so much fun that we wrote 11.

00:04:05.600 --> 00:04:10.180
Then we said let's make an album, so we're
cuttin' a record!"

00:04:10.180 --> 00:04:11.890
Taking the stage

00:04:11.890 --> 00:04:16.160
While he's been missed on the big and small
screens, Radnor has been a regular feature

00:04:16.160 --> 00:04:18.850
on popular stages for the past few years.

00:04:18.850 --> 00:04:24.720
For example, in 2015, he appeared in the Pulitzer
Prize-winning play Disgraced, and most recently,

00:04:24.720 --> 00:04:28.940
he could be seen in The Babylon Line at The
Lincoln Center Theater opposite Elizabeth

00:04:28.940 --> 00:04:30.220
Reaser.

00:04:30.220 --> 00:04:32.380
A turnaround

00:04:32.380 --> 00:04:36.510
Radnor has made some eclectic choices since
the ending of How I Met Your Mother, and while

00:04:36.510 --> 00:04:40.870
he may not be following the stereotypical
path of most actors, he's still been keeping

00:04:40.870 --> 00:04:46.780
himself busy with valuable and original projects,
like his festival-friendly drama The Seeker.

00:04:46.780 --> 00:04:50.260
Radnor's smarts and ambition should serve
him well in any field.

00:04:50.260 --> 00:04:52.940
Here's hoping we just get to see a little
bit more of him soon.

00:04:52.940 --> 00:04:54.680
Thanks for watching!

00:04:54.680 --> 00:04:57.740
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:04:57.740 --> 00:05:00.490
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
